description: Global rules for the entire e-commerce project
alwaysApply: true
Global Project Rules

Before changing anything:

Read AGENTS.md.
Read relevant project documentation.
Read docs/ROADMAP.md.
Inspect existing implementation.
Search for reusable existing functionality.
Make the smallest safe change.

Never modify unrelated code.

Never introduce unnecessary dependencies.

Never duplicate business logic.

The NestJS backend is authoritative.

Web, admin, reseller and mobile clients consume backend APIs.

Database changes require migrations.

Accounting changes require accounting tests.

Payment changes require idempotency and server-side verification.

Security-sensitive changes require security review.

After implementation:

Run relevant tests.
Run type checking.
Run linting where applicable.
Review git diff.
Report changed files and validation results.

If requirements conflict with documentation, stop and explain before making a large change.